# SOTEX ERP — Advanced Roles, Permissions & Access Control System
## Complete Arabic RTL User Management and RBAC Design Specification

---

# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Design a comprehensive enterprise-grade user management, roles, permissions, and access control module for the SOTEX ERP manufacturing system.

This module is responsible for managing every employee, administrator, manager, accountant, warehouse operator, production worker, supervisor, and external business user who accesses the ERP.

The system must control:

- Who can log in.
- Which modules users can access.
- Which pages they can view.
- Which records they can see.
- Which operations they can perform.
- Which transactions they can approve.
- Which departments they can manage.
- Which branches they can access.
- Which warehouses they can operate.
- Which financial information they can view.
- Which sensitive employee information they can access.

Create a complete visual interface for an enterprise-grade Role-Based Access Control system (RBAC), with optional data-scope restrictions and configurable approval workflows.

**The entire interface must be in Arabic and fully RTL.**

Do not create a simple list of users with a basic role dropdown. Build a complete permission management platform.

# 2. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE

The permissions system must have four separate but connected layers.

## Layer 1 — Users

Users represent the actual people who log into the ERP.

Each user has:

- User ID.
- Full name.
- Profile photo.
- Email.
- Mobile number.
- Employee ID.
- Department.
- Job title.
- Assigned branch.
- Assigned warehouses.
- Assigned roles.
- Account status.
- Last login.
- Login history.
- Account creation date.

A user may have one or multiple assigned roles, according to administrator policy.

## Layer 2 — Roles

Roles represent job responsibilities.

Examples:

- مالك المصنع.
- المدير العام.
- مدير العمليات.
- مدير الإنتاج.
- مدير المخازن.
- محاسب.
- موظف مبيعات.
- أمين مخزن.

Each role contains a predefined set of permissions.

Allow administrators to:

- Create roles.
- Edit roles.
- Duplicate roles.
- Assign permissions.
- Assign data scopes.
- Configure approval limits.
- Activate or deactivate roles.
- View users assigned to each role.
- View role activity history.

## Layer 3 — Permissions

Permissions control specific actions inside every module.

Do not define permissions only at the module level.

For example, a warehouse employee may be allowed to:

- View inventory.
- Search products.
- Create goods receiving records.
- Create stock issue requests.
- Perform assigned stock counts.

But may not be allowed to:

- Edit product costs.
- Approve stock adjustments.
- Delete inventory transactions.
- View financial reports.
- Change warehouse settings.

## Layer 4 — Data Scope

Data scope controls which records users are allowed to access.

Possible scopes:

1. كل الشركة.
2. فرع محدد.
3. قسم محدد.
4. مخزن محدد.
5. خطوط إنتاج محددة.
6. العملاء المخصصون للمستخدم.
7. المهام المخصصة للمستخدم.
8. السجلات التي أنشأها المستخدم.
9. السجلات التي يشرف عليها المستخدم.

A permission to view a page must not automatically grant access to every record in the company.

